WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.875
Step three checks the fictional tenant for
GCC, with its twenty-million-byte limit.

2
00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:09.850
Five findings and seven warnings,
and the exit code is two.

3
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.825
Read the story in the fixture.

4
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:17.821
Issuing CA 2 was renewed, so the thumbprint
the card program expects is gone from

5
00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:23.362
the trust store, and the renewed CA's
CRL is large, slow and served over HTTPS.

6
00:00:23.362 --> 00:00:26.338
A legacy intermediate has no CRL at all.

7
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:30.962
The mode rule maps the wrong
OID, so PIV is single-factor.

8
00:00:30.962 --> 00:00:34.370
And the phishing-resistant
policy is still report-only.
